-- title:
--   Each chart of X₀(Np) has reduced fibre with two components
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and $p$ a prime with $p \nmid N$. Work inside the field $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull (N * p)`, regarded as an algebra over the ring $\mathbb{Z}_\ell =$ [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) (a discrete valuation subring of $\mathbb{Q}$), and let $j \in F$ denote the element `jFull (N * p)` attached to $jq$. For a subset $S \subseteq F$, `chartAlg` is the $\mathbb{Z}_\ell$-subalgebra of elements of $F$ integral over $\mathbb{Z}_\ell[S]$; thus `chartAlgFin (N * p) p` is the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}_\ell[j]$ in $F$, and `chartAlgInf (N * p) p` the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}_\ell[j^{-1}]$ in $F$. The conclusion is a conjunction of four assertions: the quotient of `chartAlgFin (N * p) p` by the ideal generated by the image of $p$ is a reduced ring; that ideal has exactly two minimal primes (the set of minimal primes has cardinality $2$); and the same two statements hold for `chartAlgInf (N * p) p`.
--
--   This is the chart-by-chart, ring-theoretic form of the Deligne–Rapoport description of the reduction of $X_0(Np)$ at a prime exactly dividing the level: the special fibre of each of the two affine charts of the integral model is a reduced curve with exactly two irreducible components. It feeds the corresponding statement for the glued scheme [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaScheme.html#L255) and is used by the lemmas of the Deligne–Rapoport model package that identify the two minimal primes with the two valuation subrings of $F$ above $p$.
-- source:
